{{Documentation/Header}}
Links to a page on [[mw:|mediawiki.org]]. It exists so that documentation imported from MediaWiki.org keeps working here — its internal links resolve to the upstream wiki instead of redlinking locally.

When the target is the page you are already on, the label renders '''bold''' and unlinked, matching how self-links behave normally.

==Syntax==
{{T|Ll|block=1
|v1=page
|v2=label
|v3=nsp =
}}

==Examples==
{| class="dataTable"
! Code !! Result
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Ll|Help:Templates}}</nowiki></code> || {{Ll|Help:Templates}}
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Ll|Help:Templates|template help}}</nowiki></code> || {{Ll|Help:Templates|template help}}
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Ll|Help:Templates|nsp=1}}</nowiki></code> || {{Ll|Help:Templates|nsp=1}}
|}

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>1</code> || – || Page || Page title on mediawiki.org. || string || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|-
| <code>2</code> || – || Label || Display text for the link. || string || the page title ||
|-
| <code>nsp</code> || – || Strip namespace || Any value shows only the page name, dropping the namespace prefix. Ignored if a label is given. || string || – ||
|}

